abstract: "Every quantum-computing technology and every quantum machine built, announced or planned: a goal-oriented comparison of the platforms; a technology graph of self-contained technologies across ten stack layers, each on seven design attributes and connected by five edge types, with the platform architectures as paths through the layers; a brief on each technology; a register of machines as architecture instances with graded evidence in every cell; every figure tagged and traced to a dated primary source. Bilingual EN/RU, published as one interactive document."
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum error correction
  - technology landscape
  - technology graph
  - superconducting qubits
  - trapped ions
  - neutral atoms
  - photonic quantum computing
  - spin qubits
